# Build context for `data_view deploy` / `warehouse deploy`: the workspace root.
# `ouroboros` zips this directory (honouring the rules below), and BuildKit reads
# this same file from the context root. The per-app Dockerfiles build with
# workspace-relative paths (`cargo build -p <app>`), so the whole source tree
# must ship — but NOT the regenerated heavy directories.
#
# IMPORTANT: use anchored `/*` (NOT bare `*`). The deploy path packages the
# artifact with the `ignore` crate (gitignore semantics), where a bare `*`
# matches files at EVERY depth — `!dir` would re-include the directory but every
# file inside it would stay ignored. Anchored `/*` only excludes top-level
# entries, so the contents of re-included directories come back automatically.
/*

# ── Cargo workspace sources ──
!Cargo.toml
!Cargo.lock
!crates
!apps

# ── Never ship regenerated / heavy trees (rebuilt inside the image) ──
# Single shared workspace target/ is top-level (already excluded by /*), but
# guard against any nested ones too.
**/target/
**/node_modules/
**/dist/
